Difference Between append() and extend()
numbers = [1, 2]

numbers.append([3, 4])

print(numbers)
Output:

[1, 2, [3, 4]]
numbers = [1, 2]

numbers.extend([3, 4])

print(numbers)
Output:

[1, 2, 3, 4]
✅ append() adds a single item.

✅ extend() adds multiple items.

Difference Between remove() and pop()
nums = [10, 20, 30]

nums.remove(20)
print(nums)
Output:

[10, 30]
nums = [10, 20, 30]

nums.pop()
print(nums)
Output:

[10, 20]
✅ remove() removes by value.

✅ pop() removes by index (default: last item).

